  "conclusions": [
    "Two spare native buffer channels exist; spare capacity alone does not qualify the interface.",
    "Existing 47k pulldown exceeds the 20uA condition for the full-range VCC-0.1V output guarantee, even before input/PCB leakage.",
    "Higher-current AUP rows and HCS Schmitt thresholds are discrete supply rows; no interpolated local-AUX/hot guarantee has been asserted.",
    "Choose and check a stronger buffer or redesign the receiving load with an explicit disconnected-source and partial-power review before implementing the path."
  ],
  "other_required_work": [
    "Connect and qualify NF AUX source/return and AUX_VALID receiving.",
    "Integrate protection-reference, negative OV sense/OK and protected-output feedback.",
    "Insert NF combined fault into the E28 latch path by splitting its existing native fault-request net; do not short two outputs.",
    "Connect bank gate/common clamp endpoints with loading and fault-energy checks.",
    "Complete guarded module-input feed and separate force return.",
    "Resolve actual minimum GLOBAL-OFF interval and AUX-UV latch recovery; normal startup timing is not fault-recovery proof."
  ],
